# interplay_iso_four_deaths: Four tasks, each to be killed by a different trigger in turn on the root FIFO (a range past the end, continuedByNext on the last segment, a zero-length range, 59 on pipeline 0), while task 5 runs its work on child FIFO 1, rung before the first death. The first ends task 1 alone: one fault of the root FIFO, whose resume publishes the stamp. The second makes Metal assert at the commit, which ends the host process although task 2 is isolated (docs/testing.md, section 4.8): the run ends there. The rest of the program is never reached: the other two deaths, task 5's bytes against those it gives alone, the dead tasks' faulting execs, and their deletes and new services.
